{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788204082945,"sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_a0b49764274443f1a536b16b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport csv\nwith open('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv', encoding='utf-8') as fh:\n    r = csv.DictReader(fh)\n    clubs = {}\n    for row in r:\n        c = row['Club']\n        clubs[c] = clubs.get(c,0)+1\nimport unicodedata\ndef fold(s):\n    return ''.join(ch for ch in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if unicodedata.category(ch)!='Mn')\nbr = [c for c in clubs if fold(c.lower()) in ['flamengo','palmeiras','corinthians','sao paulo','gremio','vasco da gama','atletico paranaense','athletico paranaense','atletico mineiro','atletico-go','atletico goianiense','bahia','botafogo','ceara sporting club','cruzeiro','fluminense','internacional','santos','sport club do recife','fortaleza','avas','avai']]\nprint(sorted(br))\nprint(len(clubs))\n\""},"output":"['Atlético Mineiro', 'Atlético Paranaense', 'Bahia', 'Botafogo', 'Ceará Sporting Club', 'Cruzeiro', 'Fluminense', 'Grêmio', 'Internacional', 'Santos', 'Sport Club do Recife']\n652\n","metadata":{"output":"['Atlético Mineiro', 'Atlético Paranaense', 'Bahia', 'Botafogo', 'Ceará Sporting Club', 'Cruzeiro', 'Fluminense', 'Grêmio', 'Internacional', 'Santos', 'Sport Club do Recife']\n652\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"\nimport csv\nwith open('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv', encoding='utf-8') as fh:\n    r = csv.DictReader(fh)\n    clubs = {}\n    for row in r:\n        c = row['Club']\n        clubs[c] = clubs.get(c,0)+1\nimport unicodedata\ndef fold(s):\n    return ''.join(ch for ch in unicodedata.normalize('NFD', s) if unicodedata.category(ch)!='Mn')\nbr = [c for c in clubs if fold(c.lower()) in ['flamengo','palmeiras','corinthians','sao paulo','gremio','vasco da gama','atletico paranaense','athletico paranaense','atletico mineiro','atletico-go','atletico goianiense','bahia','botafogo','ceara sporting club','cruzeiro','fluminense','internacional','santos','sport club do recife','fortaleza','avas','avai']]\nprint(sorted(br))\nprint(len(clubs))\n\"","time":{"start":1788204082941,"end":1788204082943}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Clean data. Now let me write the implementation. Structure:\n\n```\nbsoccer/\n  __init__.py\n  normalization.py   # team name + date parsing\n  data_loader.py     # load 6 CSVs → Match/Player records\n  queries.py         # query engine\n  server.py          # MCP server (MCPServer from mcp 2.x)\nserver.py            # thin launcher at root: from bsoccer.server import main\ntests/\n  test_bdd.py\nrequirements.txt\nREADME.md (update briefly)\n```\n\nLet me build the alias map carefully. Canonical display names for the classic clubs (used across files):\n\nBrasileirão (36 names with suffix) → canonical:\n- America-MG → América-MG ... hmm. What should the canonical display be? I'll use a consistent style: e.g. \"Athletico Paranaense\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Atlético Goianiense\", \"América Mineiro\", \"América de Natal\", \"Vasco da Gama\", \"Sport Recife\", \"CSA\", \"São Paulo\", \"Grêmio\", \"Avaí\", \"Ceará\", \"Goiás\", \"Náutico\", \"Vitória\", \"Criciúma\", \"Paraná\", \"Atlético-GO\"...\n\nLet me define the alias map (folded key → canonical display):\n\nState suffixes: AC AL AM AP BA CE DF ES GO MA MG MS MT PA PB PE PI PR RJ RN RO RR RS SC SE SP TO\n\nClassic clubs alias entries:\n- palmeiras-sp, palmeiras → Palmeiras\n- flamengo-rj, flamengo → Flamengo\n- fluminense-rj, fluminense → Fluminense\n- vasco da gama-rj, vasco, vasco da gama, vasco da gama rj → Vasco da Gama\n- botafogo-rj, botafogo, botafogo rj → Botafogo (but Botafogo-PB exists! \"Botafogo - PB\" → key \"botafogo-pb\" — state suffix strip → \"botafogo\" — DANGER: would merge Botafogo-PB with Botafogo-RJ. So for stripping rule, require stripped name in CANONICAL set which includes \"botafogo\" → strips → wrong merge with Botafogo-PB!)\n\nHmm. Botafogo-PB is a real different club. How to distinguish? The strip rule: \"botafogo-pb\" → stripped \"botafogo\" in CANONICAL → would return \"Botafogo\". Wrong.\n\nRefine: for the strip rule, only strip when the ORIGINAL name with suffix is itself the dominant variant of the canonical club. I.e., prefer alias-map-first: register suffixed keys explicitly in the alias map for well-known clubs: \"botafogo-rj\" → Botafogo (registered), \"botafogo-pb\" → keep as-is → \"Botafogo-PB\" (register explicitly as its own canonical). Only fall back to the generic strip rule when the suffixed key is not registered. For unregistered suffixed keys, stripping is risky, so apply strip ONLY IF the stripped form is NOT itself ambiguous... \n\nSimpler and safer: NO generic stripping rule at all. Instead: build a comprehensive alias map covering all suffixed variants of the ~40 classic clubs (I know all 36 Brasileirão names + novo variants + BR-Football variants + Libertadores entries). For anything not in the map, the folded name (with suffix) is its own canonical key. Within-file consistency is preserved because names repeat exactly.\n\nBut cross-file merging for non-registered clubs (small cup teams) won't happen — acceptable.\n\nWait, but there are variants like \"América - MG\" vs \"América-MG\" vs \"America - MG\" vs \"America MG\" (BR-Football). My key normalization collapses \" - \" → \"-\", folds accents, so \"america-mg\" covers 3 of 4; \"america mg\" (space no dash) differs. Add normalization: also try replacing spaces before a 2-letter state... Simpler: normalize trailing state pattern: if name ends with a standalone state token (after space or dash), canonicalize to \"-<state>\" form: e.g. \"america mg\" → \"america-mg\"; \"vasco da gama rj\" → \"vasco da gama-rj\"; \"santos ap\" → \"santos-ap\"?? Wait \"Santos AP\" is Santos-AP (Amapá) — different from Santos! And \"Sao Jose PA\" vs \"Santos AP\". OK the trailing-state-token canonicalization handles \"america mg\"→\"america-mg\" and \"vasco da gama rj\"→\"vasco da gama-rj\" and keeps \"santos ap\"→\"santos-ap\" distinct from \"santos\". \n\nEdge: \"Vitoria EC\" vs \"Vitória\"? \"vitoria ec\" stays separate; register alias \"vitoria ec\" → Vitória? Actually \"Vitoria EC\" in BR-Football might be EC Vitória (Bahia). And \"EC Vitoria\" too. Register both → \"Vitória\". Also \"Vitoria ES\" is a different club (Vitória-ES) → keep. OK.\n\nNow the alias map — let me enumerate the classic clubs and their variants across files:\n\nFrom Brasileirao_Matches (all have -XX suffix):\n- America-MG → América Mineiro (also \"América-MG\" in novo, \"America - MG\" cup, \"America MG\" BR-F)\n- Atletico-GO → Atlético Goianiense (\"Atlético-GO\" novo, \"Atlético - GO\" cup, \"Atletico Goianiense\" BR-F, \"Atletico-GO\" cup)\n- Atletico-MG → Atlético Mineiro (\"Atlético-MG\" novo/lib, \"Atlético - MG\" cup, \"Atlético Mineiro\" cup, \"Atletico Mineiro\" BR-F)\n- Atletico-PR → Athletico Paranaense (\"Athletico-PR\" novo, \"Atlético-PR\"/\"Atlético - PR\"/\"Atlético Paranaense\"/\"Athletico Paranaense\"/\"Atletico Paranaense\" cup/BR-F, \"Athletico\" lib)\n- Avai-SC → Avaí (\"Avaí\" novo/lib, \"Avaí - SC\" cup, \"Avai\" BR-F)\n- Bahia-BA → Bahia (\"Bahia\" novo/lib, \"Bahia - BA\" cup, \"Bahia\" BR-F, \"EC Bahia\" BR-F)\n- Botafogo-RJ → Botafogo (\"Botafogo\" lib/BR-F, \"Botafogo - RJ\" cup; Botafogo-PB separate; \"Botafogo SP\" separate (BR-F); \"Botafogo RJ\" BR-F)\n- Ceara-CE → Ceará (\"Ceará\" novo, \"Ceará - CE\" cup, \"Ceara\" BR-F)\n- Chapecoense-SC → Chapecoense (\"Chapecoense\" novo/lib/BR-F, \"Chapecoense - SC\" cup)\n- Corinthians-SP → Corinthians (\"Corinthians\" everywhere)\n- Coritiba-PR → Coritiba (\"Coritiba\" novo/lib/BR-F, \"Coritiba - PR\"/\"Coritiba PR\" cup/BR-F)\n- Criciuma-SC → Criciúma (\"Criciúma\" novo, \"Criciuma\" BR-F)\n- Cruzeiro-MG → Cruzeiro (\"Cruzeiro\" lib/BR-F, \"Cruzeiro - MG\"? check cup... probably \"Cruzeiro - MG\")\n- Csa-AL → CSA