ts\n\ndef normalize_key(name):\n    - strip, collapse whitespace\n    - remove parenthetical \"(antigo ...)\" / \"(...)\" → if parenthetical is a country code (2-4 alpha uppercase), convert to -CODE suffix instead\n    - collapse \" - \" → \"-\"\n    - if ends with state token after space → convert to -STATE\n    - fold\n```\n\nWait — order matters. \"Guaraní (PAR)\": parenthetical is uppercase country code → convert to \"-PAR\": \"guaraní -par\"? Then collapse \" -\" → \"-\": \"guarani-par\". Hmm \"Guaraní (PAR)\" → replace \" (PAR)\" with \"-PAR\" → \"Guaraní-PAR\". Good. \"Nacional (URU)\" → \"Nacional-URU\". \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → parenthetical lowercase → remove → \"Boavista Sport Club  - RJ\" → collapse → \"boavista sport club-rj\".\n\nState suffix detection for canonicalization \"america mg\" → \"america-mg\": if last token (split by space) is a state abbr AND name has ≥2 tokens → join with \"-\". But \"Cuiaba MT\" → \"cuiaba-mt\" ✓. \"Sao Jose PA\" → \"sao jose-pa\" ✓ (vs \"Sao Jose - POA\" → \"sao jose-poa\" stays distinct; fine). \"Real FC\" — \"fc\" not state ✓. \"Gama\" single token — no ✓. \"River (PI)\" → paren country-code rule: \"PI\" is 2 uppercase → \"river-pi\" ✓ nice. \"River AC\" → \"river-ac\" ✓.\n\nBut wait: \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" → last token \"RJ\" state → \"vasco da gama-rj\" ✓ matches \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\". \"Botafogo RJ\" → \"botafogo-rj\" ✓ merges with \"Botafogo-RJ\" ✓. \"America FC Natal\" — no state ✓. \"Fortaleza EC\" ✓. \"Santa Cruz FC\" ✓. \"Santos AP\" → \"santos-ap\" ✓ distinct from \"santos-sp\" ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Coritiba PR\" → \"coritiba-pr\" ✓. \"Audax SP\" → \"audax-sp\" ✓. \"Aguia Negra-MS\" → already dash ✓.\n\nAlias map (folded key → canonical display name). I'll write it comprehensively for classic clubs + common variants. CANONICAL set not needed since no generic stripping — alias map only.\n\nFor display names I'll use accented proper names:\n- \"América Mineiro\" — hmm, but simpler to use common short forms: \"América-MG\"? I'll go with proper common names:\n  - America-MG variants → \"América Mineiro\"\n  - América-RN / América de Natal / América - RN → \"América de Natal\"\n  - Atletico-GO → \"Atlético Goianiense\"\n  - Atletico-MG → \"Atlético Mineiro\"\n  - Atletico-PR → \"Athletico Paranaense\"\n  - Avai → \"Avaí\"\n  - Botafogo → \"Botafogo\" (RJ)\n  - Botafogo-PB → \"Botafogo-PB\"\n  - Botafogo SP → \"Botafogo-SP\"\n  - Bragantino (SP) → \"Red Bull Bragantino\"\n  - Bragantino-PA → \"Bragantino-PA\"\n  - Ceara → \"Ceará\"\n  - Criciuma → \"Criciúma\"\n  - CSA → \"CSA\"\n  - Cuiaba → \"Cuiabá\"\n  - Goias → \"Goiás\"\n  - Gremio → \"Grêmio\"\n  - Nautico → \"Náutico\"\n  - Parana → \"Paraná\"\n  - Sao Paulo → \"São Paulo\"\n  - Sport → \"Sport Recife\"\n  - Vasco → \"Vasco da Gama\"\n  - Vitoria → \"Vitória\"\n  - Portuguesa Desportos → \"Portuguesa\"\n  - Portuguesa RJ / Portuguesa-RJ? → \"Portuguesa-RJ\"\n  - Santa Cruz → \"Santa Cruz\"\n  - EC Bahia → \"Bahia\"\n  - EC Vitoria / Vitoria EC → \"Vitória\"\n  - EC Juventude → \"Juventude\"\n  - Nautico Capibaribe → \"Náutico\"\n  - Sport Club do Recife → \"Sport Recife\"\n  - Ceará Sporting Club → \"Ceará\"\n  - Guaraní-PAR / Guaraní (PAR) → \"Guaraní (PAR)\"\n  - Athletico → \"Athletico Paranaense\"\n  - América-MG...\n  - \"Grêmio Novorizontino\" / \"Gremio Novorizontino\" → keep\n  - \"Novorizontino\" vs \"Gremio Novorizontino\" — separate, fine.\n  - \"Barueri\" — Grêmio Prudente/Barueri... skip.\n\nAlso add: \"America-RN\" (novo) → \"América de Natal\"; \"América - RN\" cup → same; \"America RN\" BR-F → same.\n\"America-MG\" novo has \"América-MG\".\n\nFIFA club names fold into the same resolver when doing cross-file queries? For player queries by club I'll just use substring matching on raw club name (per spec example: Club containing \"Flamengo\"). But also offer resolved club matching via the same normalizer: \"Ceará Sporting Club\" and \"Ceara\" — for FIFA clubs I'll apply resolve(