.compile(r\"\\s*\\(([^()]*)\\)\\s*\")\n-_TRAILING_STATE_TOKEN = re.compile(r\"^(?P<base>.+?)\\s+(?P<state>[A-Z]{2})$\")\n \n \n def _normalize_punctuation(name: str) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Canonicalize spaces/hyphens so 'América - MG' == 'América-MG'.\"\"\"\n","additions":0,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"bsoccer/normalization.py","time":{"start":1788204311259,"end":1788204311261}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Plain \"Guaraní\" never appears in Libertadores — only \"Guaraní (PAR)\" and \"Guaraní-PAR\". And \"Nacional (URU)\"/\"Nacional-URU\". Also \"Nacional (PAR)\" exists — distinct from \"Nacional (URU)\" ✓ (my paren rule: \"Nacional (PAR)\" → \"nacional-par\", stays distinct from \"nacional-uru\" ✓).\n\nSo I must REMOVE the plain \"Guaraní\" alias (would wrongly capture Brazilian Guarani from novo). Same check for \"Nacional\": plain \"Nacional\" doesn't appear. Remove `_alias(\"Guaraní (PAR)\", ..., \"Guaraní\")`. Also \"Delfín\" plain: does \"Delfín\" appear alone? Let me not risk it — keep \"Delfín-EQU\"/\"Delfín - EQU\"/\"Delfín\" — if plain \"Delfín\" appears in Libertadores it's the same club anyway; but does \"delfin\" appear in other files? BR-Football teams list didn't show Delfín. novo? No. Safe to keep plain \"Delfín\" alias? If plain \"Delfín\" appears in Libertadores it is the same club. Keep. But for Guaraní remove plain.\n\nAlso \"Barcelona (EQU)\" — plain \"Barcelona\"? Not in the list I saw (\"Barcelona-EQU\" only). My alias for Barcelona: variants \"Barcelona-EQU\", \"Barcelona - EQU\", \"Barcelona (EQU)\" — I didn't include plain \"Barcelona\". Good.\n\nOne more issue: `resolve_cache` caches ALIASES lookups — fine, but cache is keyed by folded key; ALIASES is static. OK.\n\nAnother subtlety: \"Sport\" alias → \"Sport Recife\". In BR-Football there's no plain \"Sport\" but there is \"Sport Recife\" ✓. In novo, \"Sport\" ✓ → Sport Recife. Any other \"Sport X\" collision? \"Sporting...\" doesn't fold to \"sport\" exactly. OK.\n\n\"Internacional\" alias — but \"Internacional RS\" and plain \"Internacional\" ✓. Also \"EC Internacional SC\" (BR-Football) — that's Internacional SC (Santa Maria) — folds to \"ec internacional sc\", distinct ✓.\n\n\"Confiança\": BR-Football has \"AD Confianca\" and \"Confianca\" — but is \"Confianca\" the same as AD Confiança? \"Confianca SE\" and \"Confianca\" also appear. There's also \"AD Confianca\" (Duque de Caxias). Fine.\n\nNow — big risk check: the `_TRAILING_STATE_TOKEN` regex I defined but never used. I decided to handle \"america mg\" → \"america-mg\" style via explicit aliases (\"America MG\" is in the alias list ✓, \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" ✓, \"Cuiaba MT\" ✓, \"Coritiba PR\" ✓). So the regex is unused — remove it or keep? Remove to avoid dead code. Actually wait, there might be other space-suffix variants in the cup file I haven't covered. Let me check the cup teams for space-suffix patterns after writing the loader — I'll run a coverage check: group all raw names by resolved canonical and look for suspicious canonicals that look like suffixed variants. I'll do that verification step later and extend aliases as needed.\n\nAlso remove the unused regex. Then data_loader.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0594862cc001vAmRrqjfKzJ45L","sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","messageID":"msg_0594802790015Mf3tPz85MO47u"}}
