(players)} players in {time.time()-t0:.2f}s')\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter((m.competition, m.source_file) for m in matches)\nfor k,v in sorted(c.items()): print(k, v)\nno_date = sum(1 for m in matches if m.date is None)\nprint('matches without date:', no_date)\n\"","time":{"start":1788204380064,"end":1788204380078}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — a problem with `_load_br_football` and `_load_novo` both setting competition = COMPETITION_BRASILEIRAO for novo. The novo file covers 2003-2019 Série A — same competition as Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2023). Standings for, say, 2015 would then mix both sources → double counting! I need to track the source per match (I do — source_file) and have standings compute from ONE source at a time. I'll handle that in queries: standings chooses a source file deterministically and reports it.\n\nBut also competition label: novo rows get \"Brasileirão Série A\" — for search by competition \"Brasileirão Série A\", results will include both sources. Dedupe by (date, teams, score) handles overlap. OK.\n\nAlso, `parse_date` for BR-Football: date column \"2023-09-24\" plain — good.\n\nSeason for BR-Football from date.year — but Brazilian seasons span a calendar year, fine.\n\nNow let me test loading quickly and check the alias coverage (find raw names that resolve to suspicious keys).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059496ca3001AFyepXARPHpItv","sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","messageID":"msg_059493aaa001iXIpGSPk7q3VZ3"}}
