{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788204631096,"sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_ed24bf92fd0e41d2be0041ff","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py","newString":"    def _build_indexes(self) -> None:\n        # Canonical team -> most frequent original spelling (display name).\n        spelling_counts: dict[str, dict[str, int]] = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(int))\n        self._team_matches: dict[str, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for match in self.matches:\n            self._team_matches[match.home].append(match)\n            self._team_matches[match.away].append(match)\n            spelling_counts[match.home][match.home_raw] += 1\n            spelling_counts[match.away][match.away_raw] += 1\n        self.team_display: dict[str, str] = {}\n        for team_key, counts in spelling_counts.items():\n            self.team_display[team_key] = max(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1])[0]\n        self._index_cup_rounds()","oldString":"    def _build_indexes(self) -> None:\n        # Canonical team -> most frequent original spelling (display name).\n        spelling_counts: dict[str, dict[str, int]] = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(int))\n        self._team_matches: dict[str, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n        for match in self.matches:\n            self._team_matches[match.home].append(match)\n            self._team_matches[match.away].append(match)\n            spelling_counts[match.home][match.home_raw] += 1\n            spelling_counts[match.away][match.away_raw] += 1\n        self.team_display: dict[str, str] = {}\n        for team_key, counts in spelling_counts.items():\n            self.team_display[team_key] = max(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1])[0]"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n@@ -67,8 +67,9 @@\n         spelling_counts[match.away][match.away_raw] += 1\n     self.team_display: dict[str, str] = {}\n     for team_key, counts in spelling_counts.items():\n         self.team_display[team_key] = max(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1])[0]\n+    self._index_cup_rounds()\n \n # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n # Name resolution\n # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n@@ -67,8 +67,9 @@\n         spelling_counts[match.away][match.away_raw] += 1\n     self.team_display: dict[str, str] = {}\n     for team_key, counts in spelling_counts.items():\n         self.team_display[team_key] = max(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1])[0]\n+    self._index_cup_rounds()\n \n # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n # Name resolution\n # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n","additions":1,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"bsoccer/queries.py","time":{"start":1788204631093,"end":1788204631095}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Issues to fix:\n1. `_max_cup_round` is a class attribute but needs population after load — `_index_cup_rounds` must be called in `_build_indexes`. Also `_stage_matches` is a staticmethod using class attr — fine.\n2. `_dedupe` uses `output.index(existing)` — O(n²) but n small after filtering; fine. But I set `self._dedupe_cache` inside `_dedupe` which is hacky and used in `search_matches` response: `\"deduplicated\": dedupe and total != len(self._dedupe_cache)` — this is wrong since `_dedupe_cache` gets set during the call itself. Let me restructure: `_dedupe` returns list; caller computes deduped count directly. Simplify:\n\n```python\ndeduped = self._dedupe(results) if dedupe else results\nresponse = {... \"count\": len(deduped[:limit]), \"total_matches\": total, \"deduplicated\": dedupe, ...}\n```\n\n3. In `search_players`, response includes club_summary — `club_player_summary` returns None if no roster; fine.\n\n4. `parse_date` returns tuple; used correctly.\n\n5. In `find_team` fuzzy fallback, `min(candidates, key=len)` — for \"America\" → candidates 'América Mineiro'(15), 'América de Natal'(16)... both len? \"américa mineiro\" vs \"américa de natal\" — mineiro shorter → América Mineiro. Reasonable.\n\nBut wait — there's a subtle bug: `find_team(\"Santos\")` → `self._resolve(\"Santos\")` = \"santos\" (folded, since \"santos\" isn't an alias key... wait \"Santos\" IS an alias variant of canonical \"Santos\" → ALIASES['santos'] = 'Santos' ✓). Then 'Santos' in team_display ✓.\n\n`find_team(\"Flamengo\")` → resolve → 'Flamengo' ✓ in team_display.\n\n`find_team(\"Fla\")` → resolve → 'fla' not in team_display → fuzzy: 'fla' in 'flamengo' ✓ unique → Flamengo. Good.\n\n6. `_stage_matches` uses `KnowledgeBase._max_cup_round` — need `_index_cup_rounds()` called in `_build_indexes`.\n\n7. In `standings`, `max(coverage.items(), key=lambda kv: (kv[1], -_SOURCE_PRIORITY...))` — the tie-break: prefer LOWER source priority → -priority higher ✓.\n\n8. `search_matches` response key \"deduplicated\" — fix per #2.\n\n9. `head_to_head` calls `_head_to_head_summary` with pre-deduped matches — but I pass `matches=matches` after dedupe ✓.\n\n10. `competition_statistics` with competition=None returns all comps mixed — \"competition\" field joins labels ✓.\n\n11. compare_seasons uses competition_statistics(competition, season) which includes all matching labels (serie a → both Brasileirão Série A + BR-Football Serie A) → double counting risk in aggregates (avg goals is a weighted average, acceptable-ish but match_count doubles for overlapping years). Hmm. For season-level aggregates, better to use ONE best source per season like standings. Let me rework competition_statistics: if a competition filter resolved to labels, compute per (label, source) coverage and use best source only. I'll add a helper `_select_matches(labels, season)` returning matches from the best (label, source) when labels is not None and season is not None; for broader queries (no season), just filter by labels across all sources but that double counts... For avg-goals style aggregates, dedupe handles overlapping rows (same date/teams/score) — mostly overlapping matches would dedupe! E.g., 2019 Série A: Brasileirao_Matches 380 + novo 380 — same matches, same scores, same dates (novo dates DD/MM/YYYY vs ISO → same date value) → dedupe removes 380. \n\nSo: in competition_statistics and biggest_wins, apply _dedupe always. Then match_count is honest. For standings, still pick single source (dedupe can't merge because standings needs complete season; dedupe would work too actually — same key logic. But if two sources disagree on a score for the same match (data errors), dedupe keeps both → double count in standings. Single-source selection is safer for standings).\n\nLet me apply: competition_statistics and biggest_wins dedupe. compare_seasons benefits automatically.\n\n12. `_match_sort_key` descending by date: `-(date.toordinal())` — matches without date → 0 → sorts last ✓.\n\n13. round filter: `str(round).strip()` — round param shadows builtin, fine here.\n\n14. players sort: `sort_by` might be passed as None → default 'overall' ✓ (signature default).\n\n15. In search_players, when club given and no FIFA club matches but user expects matches — response has count 0. Fine.\n\nLet me fix these issues now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0594d441f001hhE6PLEqdpxRME","sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","messageID":"msg_0594caaf7001EfrR58Yb7ktM8S"}}
