{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788204967321,"sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_a781ab62b0ca47c6b745f2c9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py","newString":"        chosen_key, _count = max(\n            coverage.items(),\n            key=lambda kv: (kv[1], -_SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(kv[0][1], 99)),\n        )\n        chosen_label, chosen_source = chosen_key","oldString":"        (chosen_label, chosen_source) = max(\n            coverage.items(),\n            key=lambda kv: (kv[1], -_SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(kv[0][1], 99)),\n        )"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n@@ -487,12 +487,13 @@\n     if match.season == season and match.competition in labels:\n         coverage[(match.competition, match.source_file)] += 1\n if not coverage:\n     return {\"error\": f\"No matches found for {competition} in season {season}.\"}\n-(chosen_label, chosen_source) = max(\n+chosen_key, _count = max(\n     coverage.items(),\n     key=lambda kv: (kv[1], -_SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(kv[0][1], 99)),\n )\n+chosen_label, chosen_source = chosen_key\n rows = [m for m in self.matches\n         if m.competition == chosen_label and m.source_file == chosen_source and m.season == season]\n \n table: dict[str, dict] = defaultdict(lambda: self._empty_stat())\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n@@ -487,12 +487,13 @@\n     if match.season == season and match.competition in labels:\n         coverage[(match.competition, match.source_file)] += 1\n if not coverage:\n     return {\"error\": f\"No matches found for {competition} in season {season}.\"}\n-(chosen_label, chosen_source) = max(\n+chosen_key, _count = max(\n     coverage.items(),\n     key=lambda kv: (kv[1], -_SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(kv[0][1], 99)),\n )\n+chosen_label, chosen_source = chosen_key\n rows = [m for m in self.matches\n         if m.competition == chosen_label and m.source_file == chosen_source and m.season == season]\n \n table: dict[str, dict] = defaultdict(lambda: self._empty_stat())\n","additions":2,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"bsoccer/queries.py","time":{"start":1788204967316,"end":1788204967319}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Coverage is correct inside, but the actual code produces matches_used=0. So the discrepancy is between my debug re-implementation and the real one... The only difference: `max(coverage.items(), key=lambda kv: (kv[1], -_SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(kv[0][1], 99)))`.\n\n`_SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(kv[0][1], 99)` — kv[0][1] is source_file string. For 'Brasileirao_Matches.csv' → 0. So key = (380, 0). For novo → (380, -3). max = Brasileirao_Matches.\n\nThen rows: `m.competition == chosen_label and m.source_file == chosen_source and m.season == season`.\n\nHmm... could `chosen_label` be unpacked wrong? `(chosen_label, chosen_source) = max(coverage.items(), ...)` — coverage.items() yields ((label, source), count) pairs! NOT (label, source) tuples directly!! `max(...)` over `.items()` returns ONE ((label, source), count) pair — a 2-tuple where element 0 is the (label, source) tuple and element 1 is the count. Unpacking `(chosen_label, chosen_source) = ((label,source), count)` gives chosen_label=(label,source) TUPLE and chosen_source=count INT!!!\n\nTHAT'S THE BUG. `chosen_label` = ('Brasileirão Série A', 'Brasileirao_Matches.csv'), `chosen_source` = 380. Then the rows filter matches nothing. And `m.season == season`... rows empty.\n\nFix: `max(coverage.items(), ...)` returns (key, count) — I need `chosen_key, count = max(...)` then `chosen_label, chosen_source = chosen_key`.\n\nSame class of bug check elsewhere: search for other `.items()` unpacking with max/min. In `_build_indexes`: `max(counts.items(), key=...)` → assigned via `max(...)[0]`? I wrote `self.team_display[team_key] = max(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1])[0]` ✓ correct.\n\nNow the stage test also returned False for cup final. `_stage_matches(cup2012[0], 'final')` — cup2012[0] might be round '1', so False is CORRECT for that particular match. The real problem earlier: search with stage='final' returned 0. That search also passed competition='Copa do Brasil' → labels {'Copa do Brasil', 'Copa do Brasil (BR-Football)'}. Filter: match.competition in labels ✓. stage filter: `match.round == KnowledgeBase._max_cup_round.get(match.season)` — `_max_cup_round` keys from `rounds[match.season] = max(rounds.get(match.season, 0), int(match.round))` — match.season for cup rows: 2012 int ✓, int(match.round) ✓ → keys {2012: '6', ...} ✓ values str ✓.\n\nWait, but is `_index_cup_rounds` actually setting `_max_cup_round`? It filters `match.competition == 'Copa do Brasil'` — the primary cup label ✓. And earlier debug printed `max cup rounds sample: {2012: '6', 2013: '8', ...}` — POPULATED ✓.\n\nSo `match.round == KnowledgeBase._max_cup_round.get(match.season)`: for a round-'6' 2012 match: '6' == '6' ✓ True. But my debug `kb._stage_matches(cup2012[0], 'final')` returned False because cup2012[0] is probably a round-1 match. So stage matching may actually work! But `search_matches(competition='Copa do Brasil', stage='final')` returned 0!! Why?\n\nThe order of filters in search_matches: stage check happens inside the same loop. Hmm — but wait, maybe the issue: `stage_q = fold(stage_query.strip())` = 'final'. First branch: `if 'final' in stage_q and 'semi' not in stage_q and '16' not in stage_q:` ✓. Then `if match.stage and ...: return True` — cup: match.stage=None → skip. `if match.competition == 'Copa do Brasil': return match.round == KnowledgeBase._max_cup_round.get(match.season)`.\n\nHmm — `KnowledgeBase._max_cup_round` — CLASS attribute access. `_index_cup_rounds` does `self._max_cup_round = {...}` → instance attribute shadows class attr. Accessing via the CLASS (`KnowledgeBase._max_cup_round`) gets the EMPTY class dict!!! THAT'S THE BUG. The instance's dict is never seen.\n\nFix: use `self._max_cup_round` (make _stage_matches a regular method) or populate the class attribute. I'll convert _stage_matches to an instance method using self._max_cup_round, and remove the class-level declaration (or keep, harmless).\n\nBoth bugs identified. Fix them.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05952657d0017hkKVImtJiv07C","sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","messageID":"msg_05951de61001WjrbxpVvDFpMSR"}}
