ctually — 68 overall for 2022 = 38+38 (both Serie A sources dedupe → 38) + cup 12 + ... let me compute: 68 - 38 = 30. Interesting — 30 = the Série A-only filtered number! Coincidence? by_competition for overall: let me debug more carefully.\n\n   Actually let me just check raw counts: Brasileirao_Matches Corinthians 2022 count, BR-Football Serie A Corinthians 2022 count.\n\n2. **Libertadores 2013 final missing one leg?** 2013 final shown once: 'Atlético Mineiro' vs 'olimpia-par' — the second leg raw might be 'Olimpia' (plain, no -par)? So the two legs have different keys ('olimpia-par' vs 'olimpia')! Check raws. If so, add alias 'olimpia' → 'Olimpia'? Hmm plain 'Olimpia' in Libertadores = Olimpia (PAR) surely. But my earlier rule: only alias when safe. 'Olimpia' plain appears only in Libertadores → safe to alias 'olimpia' → 'Olimpia (PAR)'. Let me check raw spellings.\n\n   Also '(None, Flamengo, Athletico Paranaense)' — a Libertadores final with season None! A row with missing/unparseable season? And 2020 final listed once 'Palmeiras vs Santos' (second leg with different score exists? it deduped? no—dedupe only merges identical scores; 2020 final legs: 0-1, 1-0 → both kept. Only one shown for 2020!). Hmm wait, the list shows 15 matches = count. Seasons 2013-2022 = 10 finals × 2 legs = 20 expected. Let me count: 2020:1, 2019:1, 2018:2, 2017:2, 2016:2, 2015:2, 2014:2, 2013:1, None:1 = 14... plus one more. Missing legs for 2013, 2019, 2020 + 1 None row. The None-season row: 'Flamengo vs Athletico Paranaense' — that's 2019 final leg 2? 2019 final: Flamengo 2-1 River (leg1), leg2 cancelled? Actually 2019 final was Flamengo vs River Plate, leg 1 in Buenos Aires 2-2? no... Leg1: River 0-1? Hmm. 2019 Libertadores final Flamengo won 2-1 on aggregate: leg1 Flamengo 2-1 River (Nov 23, Lima), leg2... wait it was a single final?? No — 2019: first final leg Nov 23 in Lima (Flamengo 2-1 River) and second leg Nov 30 (Flamengo 1-1 River)? No... Actually 2019 final: two legs — Nov 23: Flamengo 2-1 River Plate; Nov 30: River Plate 1-2 Flamengo?? No no. The real 2019 final: Leg 1: Flamengo 2-1 River. Leg 2: River 1-1 Flamengo? Hmm — actually it was: leg1 2-1 Flamengo (in Buenos Aires? no, Lima), leg2 1-1 (Flamengo champions 3-2 agg). Whatever — the point: some finals may have 1 or 2 rows in data, fine.\n\n   The None-season row needs checking — parse issue with some datetime value? Let me check rows where season is None in Libertadores. Also 'nacional-par'/'olimpia-par' — Nacional (PAR) = Club Nacional (Paraguay)?? Note: 2014 final was San Lorenzo vs Nacional (PAR) ✓ my paren rule made 'nacional-par' ✓ consistent. But display shows folded 'nacional-par' — unknown team, fine.\n\n   The missing 2013 leg / 2020 leg / 2019 leg — likely raw spelling variants of the same clubs creating different keys, e.g. 'Olimpia' plain vs 'Olimpia-PAR'. h2h per pair then splits. Not fatal but let me check and add aliases: 'olimpia' variants.\n\n3. Cup finals 34 includes round-8 2021 legs labeled final — 2021 cup: rounds up to 8?? 2021 Copa do Brasil format: 64 teams → 5 knockout rounds (1st/2nd/3rd/semifinal/final) = rounds '1'..'5'?? But max round for 2021 in data was... The printed finals include (2021, ABC vs Flamengo) etc. — those are ROUND 4 quarterfinals? Hmm 2021: rounds 1-2 preliminaries, R16, QF, SF, Final... The file's round numbering for 2021 may go to 6. ABC vs Flamengo happened in round 4? no — Flamengo beat ABC in... 2021 Copa do Brasil: Flamengo vs ABC was ROUND OF 16? no, ABC-Flamengo was... I recall Flamengo x ABC in 2021 was quarterfinal? Doesn't matter — the issue: my \"final = max round per season\" heuristic. 2021 max round = 6? and the final (Atlético-MG vs Athletico-PR, Dec 12/16) has round '6'? But printed finals show 8 matches for 2021 including quarterfinals — meaning max_cup_round[2021] = 4?? and those round-4 matches matched! Wait the printed list: (2021, ABC, Flamengo), (2021, Atlético Goianiense, Athletico Paranaense), (2021, CRB, Fort