iver Plate vs Flamengo at Monumental. Not 'Flamengo vs Athletico'. The glitch row is unexplainable — a data error row for some final (maybe 2021 final leg 2 Flamengo vs Athletico Nov 27/30, 2021! YES — 2021 final: Athletico-PR vs Flamengo, legs Nov 27 (1-2? Athletico 1-0?) — leg1 Athletico 1-1? The 2021 final: Athletico Paranaense 1-1 Flamengo (leg1?), leg2 Flamengo 1-2 Athletico?? Actual: 2021 final legs: Nov 27: Athletico 1-1 Flamengo? Hmm no — Athletico won 2021: leg1 Flamengo 1-1 Athletico (Nov 27), leg2 Athletico 1-0 Flamengo (Nov 30). And my earlier BR-Football data showed exactly those two legs (Nov 30 Athletico 1-0 wait it showed 'Athletico Paranaense' 1-2 'Flamengo' Oct 21?? no those were SEMIFINAL vs Flamengo... whatever). The glitch row 'Flamengo vs Athletico' with NA date/goals = probably a placeholder for a 2021 final leg. Fine — honest data gap.)\n\nSo Libertadores finals are correct. Now the cup final heuristic fix: max round with ≤2 matches per season. Also require the season to have the round as max. Implement in _index_cup_rounds: for each season, max round R; count matches in round R; if count ≤ 2 → final round = R else no final.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0595932d2001DjMsGqD1dxBEtI","sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","messageID":"msg_05958a45d001HYO5x29Tu3M7DK"}}
