{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788206047900,"sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_53c064eec2b74624adfef4b8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom bsoccer.queries import KnowledgeBase\nfrom collections import Counter\nkb = KnowledgeBase()\ntm = [m for m in kb._team_matches['Corinthians'] if m.season==2022]\nprint('raw candidates:', Counter(m.source_file for m in tm))\nded = kb._dedupe(tm)\nprint('after dedupe:', Counter(m.source_file for m in ded))\n# key-level overlap\ndef key(m): return (m.date_key(), tuple(sorted((m.home, m.away))), m.home_goal, m.away_goal)\nbm_keys = {key(m) for m in tm if m.source_file=='Brasileirao_Matches.csv'}\nbr_keys = {key(m) for m in tm if m.source_file=='BR-Football-Dataset.csv'}\nprint('BM keys:', len(bm_keys), 'BR keys:', len(br_keys), 'shared:', len(bm_keys & br_keys))\nimport datetime\n# show a few unshared\nonly_br = list(br_keys - bm_keys)[:4]\nfor m in tm:\n    if m.source_file=='BR-Football-Dataset.csv' and key(m) in only_br:\n        print('BR-only:', m.date, m.home_raw, m.home_goal, m.away_goal, m.away_raw)\n\""},"output":"raw candidates: Counter({'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 48, 'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 38, 'Libertadores_Matches.csv': 10})\nafter dedupe: Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 38, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 28, 'Libertadores_Matches.csv': 10})\nBM keys: 38 BR keys: 48 shared: 20\nBR-only: 2022-11-13 Corinthians 0 1 Atletico Mineiro\nBR-only: 2022-11-05 Corinthians 1 0 Ceara\nBR-only: 2022-10-05 EC Juventude 2 2 Corinthians\nBR-only: 2022-08-30 Corinthians 1 0 Bragantino\n","metadata":{"output":"raw candidates: Counter({'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 48, 'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 38, 'Libertadores_Matches.csv': 10})\nafter dedupe: Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 38, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 28, 'Libertadores_Matches.csv': 10})\nBM keys: 38 BR keys: 48 shared: 20\nBR-only: 2022-11-13 Corinthians 0 1 Atletico Mineiro\nBR-only: 2022-11-05 Corinthians 1 0 Ceara\nBR-only: 2022-10-05 EC Juventude 2 2 Corinthians\nBR-only: 2022-08-30 Corinthians 1 0 Bragantino\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom bsoccer.queries import KnowledgeBase\nfrom collections import Counter\nkb = KnowledgeBase()\ntm = [m for m in kb._team_matches['Corinthians'] if m.season==2022]\nprint('raw candidates:', Counter(m.source_file for m in tm))\nded = kb._dedupe(tm)\nprint('after dedupe:', Counter(m.source_file for m in ded))\n# key-level overlap\ndef key(m): return (m.date_key(), tuple(sorted((m.home, m.away))), m.home_goal, m.away_goal)\nbm_keys = {key(m) for m in tm if m.source_file=='Brasileirao_Matches.csv'}\nbr_keys = {key(m) for m in tm if m.source_file=='BR-Football-Dataset.csv'}\nprint('BM keys:', len(bm_keys), 'BR keys:', len(br_keys), 'shared:', len(bm_keys & br_keys))\nimport datetime\n# show a few unshared\nonly_br = list(br_keys - bm_keys)[:4]\nfor m in tm:\n    if m.source_file=='BR-Football-Dataset.csv' and key(m) in only_br:\n        print('BR-only:', m.date, m.home_raw, m.home_goal, m.away_goal, m.away_raw)\n\"","time":{"start":1788206047876,"end":1788206047898}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Very revealing:\n\n- 'Brasileirão Série A' 2022: 30 played — should be 38.\n- 'Série A (BR-Football)' 2022: 18 — but BR-Football Serie A 2022 Corinthians should be 38!\n- All comps: 68 = 30 + 18 + 10 + 10.\n\nSo candidates were ALREADY wrong before dedupe. _team_matches['Corinthians'] 2022 → 38 BM rows + 38 BR-Football rows?? But by_comp shows 30 + 18. Two effects: dedupe merging ACROSS sources (correct) — 38 BM + 38 BR → dedupe by (date, teams, score) → should be 38 if dates match. Result 30+18 split by label → dedupe kept BM copy for 30 fixtures and BR copy for 18 fixtures?! That means: 30 fixtures matched EXACTLY on (date, teams, score) — kept BM copy; 18 fixtures differ (different date or score) → BR copy kept separately; and BM's copy of those 18 fixtures... would ALSO be present (as a non-duplicate!) → BM count should be 30+18=38 minus nothing... but by_comp shows BM=30 only. So BM only had 30 rows for 2022?!\n\nBut my direct count said BM Corinthians 2022 = 38. Contradiction — UNLESS _team_matches wasn't built with all rows... OR the dedupe in _build_indexes (matches_unique) isn't involved here... team_statistics uses self._team_matches (raw, no dedupe) → filter → dedupe. If BM had 38 rows and BR 38 rows for the same fixtures, dedupe keeps 38 total (one per fixture) — but we see 48 (30+18). So the (date, teams, score) keys differ for 18 fixtures AND the BM copies of those 18 are MISSING.\n\nHmm wait — maybe BM 2022 has only 30 Corinthians matches and my earlier count of 38 was on the pre-fix dataset?? The earlier check: `cor = [m for m in bm if m.season==2022 and 'Corinthians' in (m.home, m.away)]` → 38 with rounds 1..38 all present. That's on canonical (post-resolve) — 'Corinthians' matches both 'Corinthians-SP' raw AND 'Corinthians' raw (BR?). But I filtered m.source_file=='Brasileirao_Matches.csv' — raws there are 'Corinthians-SP' → canonical 'Corinthians' ✓ 38 rows.\n\nSo BM has 38. Then team_statistics candidates = BM 38 + BR-Football 38 = 76 → dedupe → 48?? That means dedupe merged only 28 pairs?? and 20 dropped?! No wait — dedupe can only KEEP one per unique key: 48 unique keys out of 76. So 28 keys shared (BM+BR identical) and 20 keys unique to BR and 0 unique to BM?? That gives BM presence 28, BR 48. But by_comp shows BM 30 / BR 18. Doesn't add up.\n\nLet me debug directly instead of speculating.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05962df70001UUDAbpAXfpkA3V","sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","messageID":"msg_0596270f1001zK7UWvvqH5loqZ"}}
