d differently) + cup 10.\n- After dedupe: 38 BM + 28 BR — dedupe merged only 20; 28 BR rows remain (18 Serie A with divergent dates + 10 cup). Total unique = 76? no: 38+28+10 = 76... wait 38 BM + 48 BR + 10 Lib = 96 raw → 76 unique. The by_comp breakdown after dedupe: 'Brasileirão Série A' = 38?? but the earlier output showed 30! \n\n  The earlier run printed by_comp 'Brasileirão Série A': 30 — but NOW after dedupe counts show BM 38. The difference: earlier run was BEFORE the last edits?? I edited competition_statistics etc. but not team_statistics... OH WAIT — earlier output was from the test failure listing? The by_comp 30/18 output came from the run just before these edits — team_statistics hasn't changed since. Hmm, actually let me recheck: the run above with by_comp 30/18 was AFTER my fuzzy-find_team fix but BEFORE... no, the dedupe-in-team_statistics edit happened before that. Confusing. The CURRENT direct debug shows dedupe → 76 unique with 38 BM + 28 BR + 10 Lib.\n\n  But the earlier by_comp printed 30 + 18 + 10 + 10 = 68. And 'overall' played=68. Now dedupe says 76. The difference between then and now: I haven't touched team_statistics... wait, I DID — I moved the None-filter before dedupe (that's it). Hmm, that shouldn't change 2022 Corinthians.\n\n  OH WAIT. I see it — earlier run: `kb.team_statistics('Corinthians', season=2022)` — candidates from _team_matches['Corinthians'] — deduped to 68. Now the same computation gives 76?! Unless _team_matches changed... _build_indexes now ALSO builds matches_unique (no effect on _team_matches). Hmm, but notice: the CURRENT debug shows dedupe result 76 — the debug used the same code path `kb._dedupe(tm)`. And the earlier by_comp summed 68. Contradiction with identical code... unless the earlier run's by_comp predates the None-goal-filter change? The None filter change: candidates exclude None-goal rows before dedupe. That REMOVES rows — could only reduce, not increase (76 > 68).\n\n  Ugh, wait — I need to recount: after None-filter, BM rows with None goals? None. BR rows? None. Lib 2022 Corinthians 10 rows — goals fine.\n\n  Actually, let me recount the debug: dedupe(tm) = 76 = 38 BM + 28 BR + 10 Lib. by_comp would show Série A: 38 (BM) + 18 (BR with divergent dates!) = wait no — BR's 28 remaining = 18 Serie A + 10 cup. by_comp: 'Brasileirão Série A' = 38, 'Série A (BR-Football)' = 18, 'Copa do Brasil (BR-Football)' = 10, Lib = 10 → overall 76.\n\n  The earlier by_comp showed 30/18/10/10 = 68 — 'Brasileirão Série A' 30! That means at that moment BM candidates for Corinthians 2022 numbered only 30!! But direct count says 38!?\n\n  Unless... the earlier run was executed with a stale .pyc? I did multiple edits; pyc caching revalidates by mtime — fine.\n\n  Hmm hold on, let me recheck the earlier output — it said by_comp: {'Brasileirão Série A': 30, ...}. And home played 15. Let me just rerun team_statistics NOW and see.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059635b6c001WyA3Ugtr3ziD3y","sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","messageID":"msg_05962e3de001sw6Y7lJtix75YM"}}
