{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788206161849,"sessionID":"ses_fa6bfda21ffejsIdYbHxpf8aCL","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_77c7c693c47c4d38a369de83","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py","newString":"# Canonical competition labels, mapped to the dataset-specific labels used in\n# the unified Match records.\n_COMPETITION_GROUPS: dict[str, set[str]] = {\n    \"brasileirao\": {\"Brasileirão Série A\"},\n    \"serie a\": {\"Brasileirão Série A\", \"Série A (BR-Football)\"},\n    \"serie b\": {\"Série B (BR-Football)\"},\n    \"serie c\": {\"Série C (BR-Football)\"},\n    \"copa do brasil\": {\"Copa do Brasil\", \"Copa do Brasil (BR-Football)\"},\n    \"libertadores\": {\"Copa Libertadores\"},\n}\n\n# Reverse map: dataset competition label -> group key (first group wins).\n_LABEL_TO_GROUP: dict[str, str] = {}\nfor _group, _labels in _COMPETITION_GROUPS.items():\n    for _label in _labels:\n        _LABEL_TO_GROUP.setdefault(_label, _group)","oldString":"# Canonical competition labels, mapped to the dataset-specific labels used in\n# the unified Match records.\n_COMPETITION_GROUPS: dict[str, set[str]] = {\n    \"brasileirao\": {\"Brasileirão Série A\"},\n    \"serie a\": {\"Brasileirão Série A\", \"Série A (BR-Football)\"},\n    \"serie b\": {\"Série B (BR-Football)\"},\n    \"serie c\": {\"Série C (BR-Football)\"},\n    \"copa do brasil\": {\"Copa do Brasil\", \"Copa do Brasil (BR-Football)\"},\n    \"libertadores\": {\"Copa Libertadores\"},\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n@@ -35,9 +35,15 @@\n     \"copa do brasil\": {\"Copa do Brasil\", \"Copa do Brasil (BR-Football)\"},\n     \"libertadores\": {\"Copa Libertadores\"},\n }\n \n+# Reverse map: dataset competition label -> group key (first group wins).\n+_LABEL_TO_GROUP: dict[str, str] = {}\n+for _group, _labels in _COMPETITION_GROUPS.items():\n+    for _label in _labels:\n+        _LABEL_TO_GROUP.setdefault(_label, _group)\n \n+\n class KnowledgeBase:\n     \"\"\"In-memory knowledge graph over the six datasets.\"\"\"\n \n     def __init__(self, data_dir: str | None = None):\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bgij0ztn/retort-88bc3733b0e3/bsoccer/queries.py\n@@ -35,9 +35,15 @@\n     \"copa do brasil\": {\"Copa do Brasil\", \"Copa do Brasil (BR-Football)\"},\n     \"libertadores\": {\"Copa Libertadores\"},\n }\n \n+# Reverse map: dataset competition label -> group key (first group wins).\n+_LABEL_TO_GROUP: dict[str, str] = {}\n+for _group, _labels in _COMPETITION_GROUPS.items():\n+    for _label in _labels:\n+        _LABEL_TO_GROUP.setdefault(_label, _group)\n \n+\n class KnowledgeBase:\n     \"\"\"In-memory knowledge graph over the six datasets.\"\"\"\n \n     def __init__(self, data_dir: str | None = None):\n","additions":6,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"bsoccer/queries.py","time":{"start":1788206161846,"end":1788206161848}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There it is! Brasileirao_Matches has 8 Corinthians 2022 rows with **None goals** (late-season rows with blank goal columns — the dataset was compiled mid/late season and has empty results for Oct-Nov 2022 matches!). My team_statistics None-filter drops them → 30 played. That's CORRECT behavior for stats (you can't count unplayed/unknown results).\n\nAlso, interesting: earlier direct count `cor = 38` didn't check goals. And BM 2019 round 38 = 10 rows with... goals? If those 10 have goals they count; the 2019 round-38 gap is just missing rows.\n\nWait, actually let me check: are those 8 rows goals really blank in the CSV, or 'NA'? Either way parse_int → None. So BM 2022 covers only rounds through ~Oct (372 of 380 rows have results league-wide?). So \"Corinthians 2022 Série A = 30\" is the honest number from this dataset; BR-Football has the remaining 18 (with results). After cross-source dedupe (all-comp stats): 38+18 BR merge → only 20 date+score matches merged; the 18 divergent ones kept from BR (different recorded dates).\n\nHmm — so for team stats the most complete picture: my dedupe keeps 30 BM + 18 BR-SerieA divergent + cup + lib = 68 total. But 8 of those BM rows had None goals → filtered → 60? No wait: the None-filter happens BEFORE dedupe → BM candidates 30, BR 48 → dedupe → 30 BM + (48 - 20 shared?) ... the shared-key count was computed including BR keys matching BM keys WITH GOALS. Fine — result: overall 68 played? The earlier by_comp showed 30+18+10+10=68 ✓.\n\nSo the numbers are honest: 2022 Corinthians: 30 played in BM's Série A (8 missing results in source) + 18 BR-Série A rows that didn't date-match... BUT WAIT — those 18 BR rows include the very same fixtures as the 8 None-goal BM rows + 10 rescheduled. The dedupe can't merge a None-goal BM row (dropped) — so no double counting there ✓. But the 10 BM rows whose dates differ from BR copies... BM 30 kept + BR 18 kept = 48 Série A \"matches\" for a 38-round season — DOUBLE COUNTING 10 fixtures that both files record with different dates!!\n\nUgh. The date-mismatch problem: BM dates vs BR dates differ for some fixtures (postponed matches recorded on different dates across sources). Score-based matching without dates? Risky (reverse fixtures can share scores).\n\nGiven this is a demo benchmark, perfect cross-source reconciliation is out of scope. Decision: for SEASON-SCOPED stats/standings, prefer single-best-source (like standings does) — avoids mixed double counting entirely and yields the official 380/38 numbers where the source has them. For UNFILTERED (all seasons/all comps) aggregates, per-label single source is harder (labels span years across sources — e.g. 'Brasileirão Série A' = BM 2012-2022 + novo 2003-2019 — you need novo for 2003-2011 and BM for 2012+).\n\nSo generalize: best-source selection PER SEASON for the chosen competition labels, then union across seasons. Implementation: group candidate matches by season; for each season pick the (label, source) with most matches in that season (among labels ∩ filter); use only those matches. That yields:\n- Corinthians 2022 Série A: BM (38 rows) vs BR-Série A (48 rows!) — most matches wins → BR-Série A with 48?! BM 38 is the correct one. BR 48 > 38 → picks BR → 48 played — WRONG (double counted within BR? BR Serie A 2022 Corinthians = 38 rows + cup? no cup is separate label. 38? earlier debug: BR keys 48 total including 10 cup → BR Serie A = 38). So per (label, source): ('Brasileirão Série A', BM) = 38 rows (incl. 8 None-goal) vs ('Série A (BR-Football)', BR) = 38. Tie → priority → BM → 38 rows → 30 with results + 8 None → stats played=30. Consistent and honest!\n\n- Corinthians 2022 all comps: per-season selection with labels=None (no competition filter): all (label, source) pairs?? With labels=None, coverage per season includes every label+source for that season: BM Série A 38, BR Série A 38, BR cup 10, BM? cup 2022 none (BM is league only), Lib 10 (single source). Season 2022: pick max per label? If we pick ONE source per season globally, we'd drop cup+Lib. Need per-label-source: for each (label, source) with matches in that season... but then BM+BR both included → 76 again.\n\n  Compromise: when sea